[h1]Fouru's ModLib — v2.3.00[/h1]
A shared framework library used by my mods (e.g. [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3161035078]Taoist[/url]). It does nothing on its own — it just lets other mods run.

[h2]⚠ Installation[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe, then [b]move ModLib to the TOP of your mod list[/b] (above every mod that uses it).
[*][b]Restart the game[/b] after changing the load order.
[*]Mods that need a newer ModLib tell you so on the title screen.
[/list]

[h2]Features (for players)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Save-safe:[/b] mod data is stored in separate JSON files and never written into your save file, so removing a mod will not break your save.
[*]Mod data of saves you delete in the game is cleaned up automatically.
[*][b]Faster:[/b] the monthly events of the mods are dispatched faster, and the mod data is saved in the background (only the files that changed).
[*]Child mods load and update in a fixed order, so they do not conflict with each other.
[*]Translations: each mod's text can be replaced through LocalText.json.
[/list]

[h2]Features (for modders)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Event system:[/b] one ordered event model for game, map, battle, UI and timers (including a monthly tick), with conditions and delayed execution.
[*][b]Persistence:[/b] global and per-save caches as plain JSON (no encryption), so they are easy to inspect and debug.
[*][b]Data sharing:[/b] child mods can exchange data, and each mod gets its own Parameter Store.
[*][b]Configs:[/b] create or replace game configs from JSON, with sample templates for every config type.
[*][b]UI framework:[/b] build windows, buttons, inputs and other controls in code.
[*][b]Icons in texts:[/b] write the game's icons (spirit stones, herbs, ores, stats...) in any localized text with [icon:NAME].
[*][b]Dramas and portraits:[/b] open dialogs with options and backgrounds; draw characters with the game's portrait art.
[*][b]Battle helpers:[/b] damage, skills, the game's visual effects, the battle scene and camera.
[*][b]Helpers:[/b] units, items, async and delay functions, Workshop descriptions as rich text, UI automation for tests, and more.
[*][b]Debug and logging:[/b] several log levels, error dialogs, and timing info.
[/list]

[h2]Open source[/h2]
You are free to build your own mod on top of ModLib (MIT license). A like is always appreciated!
[list]
[*][b]Source code, docs and how to create a mod:[/b] [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-ModLib/]https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-ModLib/[/url] (ModLib internals, a sample of every game config, the game's icons and effects)
[*][b]A complete example mod:[/b] [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/]https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/[/url] (the Taoist mod with its build, deploy and test scripts, and a step-by-step guide)
[/list]

